<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maravarman Sundara Pandya I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1216">1216</a>–<a href="/years/1238">1238</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maravarman Sundara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> I was a king of the Later Pandya dynasty who began the revival of Pandya power in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Around 1219 he invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> kingdom, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uraiyur">Uraiyur</a> and forced the Chola king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulottunga-iii">Kulottunga III</a> to submit. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> intervention restored the Cholas, but his campaigns opened the way for later Pandya supremacy in the Tamil country.</p></div>
